Title: worktree-gc: design a safe age/mtime husk-removal heuristic (deferred from 0325)
Created: 2026-07-14
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-07-14T13:05Z claude created
2026-07-14T20:09Z claude note decision: report-only-forever — /proc cwd probe not permission-independent (EACCES=ENOENT), remote sessions undetectable, live near-miss on the raid session's own husk

--- body ---
## Context
Ticket 0325 made `scripts/worktree-gc.sh` **report** unregistered husk dirs
under `.claude/worktrees/` (dirs that are no longer registered git worktrees).
It deliberately stopped at report-only — a husk may be a LIVE session's base
cwd (the harness resets the shell cwd there after every command), so blind
removal breaks that session. 0325 Action 2 left an open design question:
"Remove a husk only when it is safe ... age/mtime threshold." A review of PR
#602 (0325) recommended tracking that removal half as a follow-up rather than
losing it.

## Relevant files
- `scripts/worktree-gc.sh` — holds the report-only husk scan from 0325; any
  removal logic would extend the scan block near the `worktree-gc: husk …` line
- `tests/test_worktree_tools.py` — `test_gc_reports_*_husk_*` cases; a removal
  test belongs beside them
- `tickets/0325-worktree-gc-detect-unregistered-husk-dir.erg` — parent ticket
  that established report-only

## Actions
1. Decide whether automatic husk removal is worth the risk at all — report-only
   may be the correct permanent answer (the 0325 red-team leaned that way).
2. (moot — decision was report-only-forever) If pursued, design a provably-safe heuristic: e.g. mtime older than a
   generous threshold AND no live session's base cwd points at it. Establish how
   to detect "live base cwd" reliably (a husk's git commands resolve to the
   primary repo, so there is no cheap in-tree signal — this is the hard part).
3. (moot — removal not implemented) Red-first test proving a fresh/live husk is NEVER removed and only a stale,
   provably-dead one is.

## Invariants
- Never remove a husk that could be a live session's base cwd.
- Report-only behavior from 0325 must remain the default.

## Verification
- [x] Decision recorded (remove-with-heuristic vs report-only-forever): report-only-forever
- [x] If removal implemented: red-first test proves a fresh/live husk survives (N/A — removal was not implemented; decision is report-only-forever)
- [x] `make check` passes

## Exit criteria
- A documented decision (remove-with-heuristic vs report-only-forever), and if
  removal is implemented, a test that proves it cannot touch a live husk.
